                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "233411346",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198404255015",
                            "num_reviews": 127,
                            "playtime_forever": 341,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 341,
                            "last_played": 1784986717
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Usually I am a huge GB Patch Games fan but this one just simply didn't hit the spot for me. The writing is good but I found it hard to connect the with the characters - especially the main character. In fact the obsession of the seer is terrifying and it made me uncomfortable the way they interacted with their love interest. The concept is a cool idea in theory, I just don't think it was executed well. Worldbuilding is also interesting in theory but you kinda just get thrown into it and half the time I didn't know what was going on. I also felt like the pacing was so off - it was antagonizingly slow at times and felt extremly repetitive since it often felt like all they do is sit around and snack, talking without saying anything interesting at all. Eventually I found myself just kind of skipping through dialouge because I got bored. The character art and UI is extremly gorgeus and the quality of the writing itself is still very good. I suppose the story itself is just what didn't hook me. It won't hurt if you play this one, but you also won't miss out on anything if you don't play it.",
